  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Horticulture trade mission Ethiopia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this mission is to strengthen Dutch-Ethiopian business partnerships in the horticulture and (agro)logistics sectors by facilitating market entry, investment, and technology transfer opportunities that contribute to a more sustainable and competitive horticulture sector in Ethiopia.Project SummaryEthiopia&#x2019;s horticulture sector is one of the country&#x2019;s fastest-growing industries, offering strong potential for collaboration with Dutch companies known for their advanced greenhouse systems, logistics, and sustainable production technologies. Despite this growth, the sector faces challenges in climate-resilient production, cold chain logistics, and access to modern inputs, technology and expertise.The Netherlands Embassy in Addis Ababa has maintained long-standing engagement in supporting Ethiopia&#x2019;s horticulture development. To seize this momentum, this project is planning to organise a Horticulture and Logistics Trade Mission composed of credible Dutch companies to Ethiopia around HortiFlora 2026, a trade fair that brings together international and Ethiopian companies, knowledge institutions, and government stakeholders. Through sector discussions, matchmaking, trade fair participation, field visits, and networking events, the mission will create a platform for Dutch companies to explore market potential, identify concrete business opportunities and strengthen bilateral cooperation.The project addresses the need for post-harvest systems, relevant inputs, reliable logistics, and technology-driven production models that can enhance production, quality and sustainability. The mission will take place in Addis Ababa and key horticulture clusters such as in Debre Zeit, Ethiopia.</narrative>
  </description>
